WEBVTT

01:03.020 --> 01:09.520
<b><i>Secondary Mutation</i></b>

01:09.230 --> 01:11.360
Charles, Hisako is fine.

01:12.030 --> 01:15.410
We've retrieved all the mutant children
who were kidnapped.

01:16.910 --> 01:18.660
Fluids...

01:19.160 --> 01:20.870
fluids...

01:21.660 --> 01:24.330
fluids!!

01:28.170 --> 01:28.960
Hisako!

01:48.350 --> 01:49.400
What is this?

01:53.110 --> 01:55.450
What is going on?

01:57.450 --> 01:59.240
Give me...

02:00.660 --> 02:02.950
my fluids back!

02:09.500 --> 02:11.130
It's a secondary mutation, Emma!

02:12.300 --> 02:13.590
Secondary mutation!?

02:16.220 --> 02:17.340
It's happening to her now!?

02:17.340 --> 02:17.930
Emma!

02:19.800 --> 02:22.350
What the hell is
with those guys!?

02:26.430 --> 02:27.850
Leave this to us.

02:29.230 --> 02:32.440
Fluids!

03:10.650 --> 03:11.810
Where'd he go?

03:11.810 --> 03:12.690
He's gone...

03:59.440 --> 04:00.490
Fluids!

04:01.070 --> 04:03.070
I want your fluids!

04:04.780 --> 04:07.200
I won't let anyone...

04:07.700 --> 04:11.710
take my fluids...

04:18.960 --> 04:20.590
What just happened to me?

04:22.050 --> 04:23.590
Are you okay, Emma!?

04:31.310 --> 04:33.060
These readings confirm it...

04:33.060 --> 04:34.850
it's a secondary mutation.

04:35.350 --> 04:38.270
Thankfully, it looks like it's
under control, for now.

04:38.820 --> 04:39.690
I...

04:40.230 --> 04:41.530
There's some variation,

04:41.530 --> 04:45.950
emotions can sometimes trigger what
causes some people to transform.

04:45.950 --> 04:49.990
Wanting to protect Hisako so desperately
must have caused it for Emma.

04:49.990 --> 04:53.160
However, once you've transformed,

04:53.160 --> 04:59.340
there is a greater chance that, someday,
you will lose control and become a monster.

04:59.340 --> 05:04.880
It's a disease for mutants
called the Damon-Hall Syndrome.

05:05.550 --> 05:08.300
The Damon-Hall Syndrome...

05:08.300 --> 05:11.600
The transformation doesn't always cause
the symptoms to appear,

05:11.600 --> 05:14.060
but you need a vaccine
to treat them.

05:14.060 --> 05:15.020
Emma...

05:38.290 --> 05:39.170
Hisako!

05:39.630 --> 05:40.590
Mom!

05:41.590 --> 05:42.460
Mom!

05:45.550 --> 05:47.720
I'm really grateful...

05:47.720 --> 05:49.220
it's all thanks to you.

05:49.220 --> 05:51.260
I wasn't sure if we'd get
Hisako back...

05:51.930 --> 05:53.810
I'm sorry, Mr. lchiki.

05:53.810 --> 05:57.310
I should have contacted you
as soon as I arrived in Japan.

05:57.980 --> 06:01.360
I was honestly pretty shocked when
Mr. Beast asked me about you...

06:01.360 --> 06:03.860
I'm glad you're alright too.

06:03.860 --> 06:07.070
Hearing that you were with
Hisako helped us relax a little.

06:09.530 --> 06:10.490
Hisako!

06:12.160 --> 06:14.040
Hisako!

06:18.000 --> 06:20.630
O-ow!

06:21.170 --> 06:23.800
I was so worried!

06:24.210 --> 06:25.630
I'm so glad you're okay!

06:26.130 --> 06:28.220
This is one of Hisako's best friends,
and her classmate.

06:28.630 --> 06:30.010
Is she a mutant?

06:30.600 --> 06:35.100
No, just a really nice girl with
no mutant prejudices.

06:35.810 --> 06:37.980
It's good to know that she
has someone like that...

06:37.980 --> 06:41.900
You start thinkin' that everyone out there
has a beef with mutants, sometimes.

06:45.900 --> 06:49.610
This should mean that no more
children will go missing too.

06:50.570 --> 06:52.620
It's all thanks to you!

06:52.620 --> 06:57.040
I'm getting dinner ready,
so please stay a bit and join us.

06:57.960 --> 06:59.330
Dear, lend me a hand.

06:59.920 --> 07:00.540
Okay.

07:16.890 --> 07:20.690
I'd like to take Emma back to
New York as soon as possible.

07:21.730 --> 07:24.110
Take me to New York?

07:25.440 --> 07:26.400
Yes.

07:26.400 --> 07:29.950
I'd like to run full tests
on you at the Xavier Institute.

07:30.820 --> 07:31.950
I'm against this.

07:32.490 --> 07:35.620
Taking her to the Institute
is out of the question...

07:36.540 --> 07:42.000
We never found any kind of tech that could
block Cerebro in the U-Men's base.

07:42.000 --> 07:44.290
And what exactly does that
have to do with me?

07:45.000 --> 07:48.460
It means that someone else
was blocking Cerebro

07:48.460 --> 07:49.880
from detecting mutant activity!

07:50.590 --> 07:52.550
And you think it was me?

07:54.350 --> 07:55.850
Enough!

07:55.850 --> 07:57.100
I've already told you.

07:57.100 --> 07:59.890
I'm not involved with
the Inner Circle any more.

07:59.890 --> 08:04.810
Besides, I'm not a strong enough telepath
to jam a system like that.

08:04.810 --> 08:05.650
But you were-

08:05.650 --> 08:07.530
The food's ready...

08:12.570 --> 08:15.740
Cyclops, I believe Emma.

08:15.740 --> 08:20.290
Look, she transformed because she was
trying to protect Hisako.

08:21.040 --> 08:26.420
They say that every mutant transforms
differently depending on its abilities.

08:26.420 --> 08:29.960
Anything we learn could help protect
other mutants in the future.

08:30.340 --> 08:34.930
Very well, I'll oblige Beast's wishes and
go to New York to be examined.

08:36.640 --> 08:41.980
To be honest, I'm still shocked that I
developed a secondary mutation...

08:44.020 --> 08:48.270
Um, does she really have to go
to New York for her examination?

08:48.690 --> 08:49.530
Yes.

08:50.110 --> 08:52.950
Plus, the Xavier Institute is

08:52.950 --> 08:56.410
the only place we can get the vaccine
that I developed

08:56.410 --> 08:58.700
for the Damon-Hall Syndrome.

08:59.620 --> 09:01.830
Then, I'll go too.

09:02.080 --> 09:02.830
Hisako!?

09:03.540 --> 09:07.420
It looks like my powers have
awakened for real this time,

09:07.420 --> 09:09.920
and without Emma
I'm not sure if I can...

09:15.260 --> 09:20.350
I'd like to ask if you'd be willing to let
Hisako come with me to New York.

09:20.350 --> 09:22.020
Well, we...

09:22.020 --> 09:25.390
I'd like to continue Hisako's training,

09:25.390 --> 09:29.230
and there's no guarantee that she won't have
to worry about a secondary mutation either.

09:29.230 --> 09:33.190
I suppose it's not a bad idea
to get the vaccine now.

09:33.190 --> 09:33.860
True.

09:34.950 --> 09:36.070
Okay.

09:36.070 --> 09:38.120
As long as you're with Emma, okay?

09:38.660 --> 09:40.740
That's great, isn't it Hisako?

09:43.000 --> 09:43.830
Yeah!

09:43.830 --> 09:44.870
Thanks.

09:45.330 --> 09:47.370
It's alright, isn't it Cyclops?

09:51.670 --> 09:52.550
Yeah.

10:20.870 --> 10:24.950
I'd love to see a musical on Broadway
while I'm in New York.

10:24.950 --> 10:29.750
It's just a short drive from
the Xavier Institute to Manhattan.

10:29.750 --> 10:32.250
Once Emma's examination is done,
we can go whenever you'd like.

10:32.250 --> 10:33.090
Really!?

10:37.680 --> 10:40.510
There's an unidentified reading coming
up on the radar on the left...

11:02.580 --> 11:03.870
It passed us!?

11:03.870 --> 11:06.080
Couldn't get a visual on it...

11:18.550 --> 11:19.970
Lemme at 'im!

11:19.970 --> 11:20.800
Take care of it!

11:23.100 --> 11:25.180
Are we going to die?

11:25.180 --> 11:26.060
It'll be fine...

11:33.650 --> 11:35.190
It can't take much more!

11:35.190 --> 11:35.940
Hurry!

12:35.920 --> 12:36.960
Gotcha!

13:47.030 --> 13:48.320
He's a mutant...

13:48.320 --> 13:50.580
From the way he was going nuts,

13:50.580 --> 13:55.410
he might even have
Damon-Hall Syndrome himself.

13:56.040 --> 13:57.250
It looks like it...

13:58.080 --> 14:02.500
This boy was in the Inner Circle's
preparatory school for mutants...

14:02.500 --> 14:03.460
What!?

14:03.920 --> 14:06.510
Hey, remember me?

14:07.800 --> 14:12.060
His body might have settled down,
but his head's still messed up.

14:12.060 --> 14:16.810
He's exhibiting all the telltale
symptoms of Damon-Hall Syndrome.

14:16.810 --> 14:17.900
The poor boy.

14:18.400 --> 14:22.110
When I first met him,
he had the most angelic face...

14:22.110 --> 14:25.820
Actually, I believe he said that
he was from Tohoku.

14:26.320 --> 14:30.280
Does this kind of thing
happen to all mutants?

14:30.280 --> 14:32.120
Is this gonna happen to me?

14:34.370 --> 14:37.000
The X-Men will be able to help you.

14:37.000 --> 14:38.040
I'm sure.

14:38.920 --> 14:43.840
We'll do our best to find out
why this is happening at the Xavier Institute.

15:00.520 --> 15:06.820
Emma Frost, Hisako lchiki,
welcome to the Xavier Institute.

15:06.820 --> 15:08.360
I'm Professor X.

15:08.950 --> 15:10.280
It's nice to meet you.

15:11.490 --> 15:14.030
Now that you're here,
you're part of the family.

15:15.040 --> 15:17.080
Make yourself at home.

15:17.660 --> 15:18.660
Very well.

15:18.660 --> 15:20.170
Thank you!

15:28.550 --> 15:30.510
It'll take a few hours
for me to finish this...

15:31.140 --> 15:34.260
It's been a long trip,
you should all get some rest.

15:34.680 --> 15:36.850
Sounds good to me.

15:36.850 --> 15:38.560
Don't work too hard, Beast.

15:42.770 --> 15:43.400
Hey!

15:46.900 --> 15:47.780
Calm down!

16:12.260 --> 16:13.340
No way...

16:14.300 --> 16:15.800
how could that!?

16:17.220 --> 16:18.680
It's alright, Hisako.

16:38.660 --> 16:42.330
What did the Inner Circle
do to him, Emma?

16:43.000 --> 16:44.080
Nothing, really.

16:44.670 --> 16:48.960
Except reinforcing his mutant powers
and mind control abilities.

16:48.960 --> 16:50.710
Is that really it?

16:50.710 --> 16:51.800
Yes.

16:51.800 --> 16:54.550
We didn't perform any experiments,
like the U-Men were doing.

16:54.550 --> 16:57.850
Although, after that battle
in which Jean died,

16:57.850 --> 17:00.270
I'm not sure what's become
of their preparatory school...

17:01.770 --> 17:05.770
I'd heard that the Inner Circle
split up after our battle.

17:06.610 --> 17:09.690
Maybe he had gone home
to Tohoku?

17:10.190 --> 17:13.450
Which'd mean there's a good chance
he was in the U-Men's base...

17:13.820 --> 17:19.080
But when he was being examined,
there was no sign of any experiments.

17:19.080 --> 17:21.370
That's right, he hasn't been
experimented on.

17:22.200 --> 17:25.250
I just finished the results
of his blood test...

17:25.250 --> 17:27.960
It's not clear if he was
ever held captive by the U-Men,

17:27.960 --> 17:31.510
but it looks like his secondary mutation
wasn't caused by an experiment,

17:31.510 --> 17:34.130
and was caused by
some other kind of stimulus.

17:34.840 --> 17:37.640
Suddenly triggered by
an unknown cause?

17:39.640 --> 17:42.640
I dunno what's going on,
but I don't like it.

17:43.350 --> 17:45.940
Well, Emma,
let's begin your examination.

17:45.940 --> 17:46.650
Right.

18:20.850 --> 18:21.640
Don't go in!

18:21.810 --> 18:22.640
Don't go in!

18:22.640 --> 18:23.430
You better not!

18:28.310 --> 18:28.980
Hey!

18:29.400 --> 18:30.110
No cheating!

18:32.900 --> 18:33.530
Yes!

18:35.820 --> 18:38.200
That's Scott's third win in a row...

18:38.570 --> 18:39.780
Thanks!

18:39.780 --> 18:41.370
I get free meals for
the next three days now.

18:42.870 --> 18:43.990
Dammit!

18:43.990 --> 18:44.790
One more time!

18:44.790 --> 18:46.410
I'll bet my motorcycle.

18:46.410 --> 18:49.500
You want to bet on
the Blackbird this time?

18:52.380 --> 18:57.340
I wanted to check with Cerebro and see
if Tohoku was back to normal again...

18:58.220 --> 19:00.840
But it's still being
blocked somehow.

19:00.840 --> 19:02.050
What!?

19:19.110 --> 19:21.410
Let's get an MRI next.

19:35.750 --> 19:37.630
Are you waiting for Emma?

19:39.220 --> 19:40.680
Yes.

19:42.970 --> 19:46.470
Oh, there was something
I'd like to ask you.

19:46.470 --> 19:47.720
What is it?

19:51.020 --> 19:53.900
Have you ever heard of
the Sasaki Institute?

19:54.440 --> 19:57.730
I think I might have heard
the name before...

19:57.730 --> 20:03.660
but it was from when I was little,
so I don't really remember.

20:04.370 --> 20:05.030
I see.

20:05.620 --> 20:06.540
Thank you.

20:23.510 --> 20:24.640
How'd it go!?

20:24.640 --> 20:28.720
Emma has the same X-Antibody
that poor boy had.

20:30.140 --> 20:33.560
Then is the same thing
going to happen to her!?

20:33.560 --> 20:35.190
You don't need to worry.

20:35.730 --> 20:37.770
My case is apparently benign.

20:44.360 --> 20:46.240
Thank goodness.

20:54.790 --> 20:56.710
We haven't eaten anything.

20:56.710 --> 20:58.040
You must be hungry.

20:58.590 --> 21:01.010
Let's go and get something to eat!

21:01.840 --> 21:02.880
Yay!

21:05.340 --> 21:06.600
Just as I suspected.

21:07.510 --> 21:12.060
Both that boy and Emma manifested
a secondary mutation in Tohoku.

21:12.060 --> 21:16.480
And we're still unable to
detect mutants there...

21:18.190 --> 21:20.780
Something is still
going on in Tohoku.

21:22.280 --> 21:25.360
I don't think this is over yet...

23:04.670 --> 23:09.220
Emma and Hisako are welcomed
as members of the X-Men.

23:09.800 --> 23:14.010
Hisako is hesitant in her training when
she realizes how powerful she is.

23:14.970 --> 23:18.730
Meanwhile, Emma agrees to open
her mind to Professor X,

23:18.730 --> 23:21.770
to clear up Cyclop's suspicions.

23:22.610 --> 23:26.320
What truths about Emma
will the X-Men learn?

23:27.490 --> 23:30.030
Next time on X-Men: Unity.

23:27.740 --> 23:31.160
<b><i>Power - Unity</i></b>
